  {
    "number": 452,
    "title": "Share bounded session titles and project names across Hub metadata",
    "body": "## Problem and resulting change\n\nRefs #424. Shared sessions currently expose a label or ID even when the provider has a title. Lifecycle 1.1 adds bounded title/source and project display metadata; the owner persists it and Hub HTTP/MCP and B.U.N.N.Y. expose snapshot 1.2. Explicit user labels retain precedence. Default snapshot 1.0 and opt-in 1.1 retain their closed shapes.\n\n## Scope and dependencies\n\nThe owner approved the field design before producer changes ([decision](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/issues/424#issuecomment-5843666785)). Titles allow 160 Unicode scalars; labels/projects allow 80. Hook configurations explicitly opt into lifecycle 1.1; existing configurations stay 1.0. Policy permits the scoped content while excluding credentials; #425 prompt/response/transcript-content capture is not implemented.\n\nSource-only: no installed hooks, settings changes, live migration, agent sessions or device operations. Hub #426, Pixoo #106 and Nanoleaf #179 adopt the released prerequisite separately. Package candidates are lifecycle 1.1.0, agent-state 3.3.0 and Hub 0.4.0. Historical vendor archives and source pins are unchanged. Publication follows guarded merge and verified main CI, with immutable checksums and source receipts.\n\nState/recovery walkthrough: the existing owner and exclusive storage lease remain authoritative. The new reader limits files to 1 MiB, 8,192 lines, 64 KiB per record and 100 ms inside the existing process deadline, with at most four unsettled reads. Missing metadata preserves lifecycle delivery. Rename fixtures show that metadata-only updates do not refresh lifecycle evidence; explicit user labels survive agent labels and legacy import. Durable 2.1 imports 1.0/2.0; older owners cannot reopen 2.1. Any separately authorized deployment must preserve its pre-upgrade export, and recovery after new writes requires a compatible owner. No device writer changes.\n\n## Validation\n\nPassed on Node 24.21.0 / Python 3.14.4:\n\n- Build/typecheck, controller contracts in TypeScript/Python and package checks.\n- Lifecycle and agent-state TypeScript/Python corpora, provider/hook fixtures, migration/restart/freshness tests and isolated reproducible package checks.\n- MCP unit/protocol/package; Hub unit/package/MCP/setup checks.\n- Agent-status, Tidbyt TypeScript/Python, LIFX and local-controller suites.\n- Dashboard checks and full browser suite, including synthetic desktop/mobile title/project previews, explicit-label precedence, Unicode label bounds, search and untitled fallback.\n- Workflow checks/tests; all 18 specifications validate. Six contract/implementation deltas synchronized and archived; the dashboard layout update modifies the same dashboard capability.\n- Pinned Pixoo `28f4875b7a0f0e57ca6f25d9971e125e927a5503` and Nanoleaf `f3c13843f1e5431b01ddca344a91cd7484348f59` source checks: handoff, independent acknowledgments, late events and legacy/latest-state rollback. Simulator/disposable state only.\n\nTidbyt Python initially lacked Pillow; rerun passed using requirements-contracts.txt in an isolated test environment. Local receipts are under the coordinator's `.local/evidence/gh-424-session-titles/`.\n\n## Dashboard candidate\n\nThe owner requested less text and better use of the right column. Sessions now start beside compact device controls; mobile puts sessions first. A feed indicator replaces the Collector card. Session diagnostics and label editing sit under Details, while attention, retained notices, command outcomes and stale evidence remain visible. Status information opens on hover/focus or touch and dismisses with Escape. Brightness meters show only known values.\n\nThe existing mode/power controls retain their command lifecycle. Browser tests open Details before editing labels; no command or conflict assertion was removed. Synthetic previews are recorded under `dashboard-compact` in the coordinator's evidence directory. Explicit approval of this revised UI candidate is required before merge.\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nUI approval, guarded merge, merged-main CI and immutable package publication remain pending. #424 stays open because installed Codex Desktop and Claude observations are not authorized or verified by source fixtures. Goal 4 retains guide assessment sections; no guide refresh is part of this PR. Downstream consumers start after the shared prerequisite is delivered.\n\n## Fixed comparison and independent reviews\n\nBase/merge-base: `0a1af41d2d5440aa40ec6353116ff4d40d982fcf`. Final head: `3bc2e0c408bee9bf89e8c03cfbf330e58abb39e1`; clean worktree. Both fresh independent Standards and Specification reviewers pass this exact head with no remaining findings.\n\nStandards found a P2 mobile tooltip overflow at `db81cd2`; the final commit clamps its position and adds a failing-before/passing-after touch test with a wrapped title. The reviewer independently verified widths 320, 390 and 900, including resize while open, Escape dismissal and zero device writes. Specification independently ran 35 Node and five Python tests; Standards ran 52 dashboard and 11 metadata tests. The full local browser suite passed before the focused tooltip correction; its focused browser, type, unit and reproducible Hub package checks pass afterward. All six exact-head hosted CI jobs passed; each job and its annotation endpoint was read, with no annotations. All 18 specifications validate; the UI delta is synchronized and archived.\n",
    "state": "open",
